00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.930
I like to give a
quick overview of

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.750
higher ed in general.
This is, maybe,

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:20.470
boring for people.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:24.580
But I imagine many of you
have gone to a university somewhere

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.270
around the world. And
you've had some post-secondary education.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.460
And universities are--

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.520
they seem like they're
like this one thing.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.870
But what a University is,

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.620
is it's just this collection
of thousands of tiny,

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:42.340
little units. And there's
this famous joke that's,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.560
we're hundreds or thousands
of little micro units,

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.580
that are all unified
by a common disagreement over

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.890
parking or a
common disagreement over the

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.860
temperatures in buildings or
a common disagreement over our

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.030
football team or whatever.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:58.870
But let me just give you
a quick sense of what--

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.090
the president of the University
of California, in the

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:03.100
'60s, was a guy
named Clark Kerr.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.650
And he referred to the
modern university as a multi

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:10.600
university. So let me just
quickly tell you why we're here.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.880
The University of Colorado
is a research university.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.410
We have three missions.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:18.220
Our three missions are to
engage in research and to

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.310
create new knowledge
out in the world,

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:25.510
to teach and

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.800
pass that knowledge
on to students,

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.920
and then finally, to
engage with the public,

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.720
in what's called the
public engagement mission.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.660
And that's translating your
research efforts into things

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.550
that can be broadly valuable.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:40.540
And that really aligns
very closely with what

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.870
open-source tools do.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:47.950
But we also do a lot more.
We produce art and creative

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.410
works. We act as a venue
for all kinds of things.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.640
We're a community space.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.120
We have a football
team. We have museums.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.540
We have a bowling alley.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.750
We provide health care
and patient treatment.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.430
We, at least at CU Boulder,

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:03.490
put a lot of stuff
into outer space.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:06.790
We engage in economic
development with the community,

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.680
here in Boulder, and
the state of Colorado,

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.270
and internationally.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.760
We-- at least at CU,

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:17.740
we care and feed and
sustain a live Buffalo, named Ralphie,

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.760
who runs around on
the football field.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:24.580
So the number of things
that a single university are engaged

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:26.570
in are quite limitless.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:29.560
And so why I like to lead
with this whole spiel is that each

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:32.410
one of those
results in a very--

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:36.910
almost limitless number
of interesting data science

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.080
questions and problems.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.010
So that's the intro.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:45.520
And I definitely want to take
most of the time to answer

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.380
questions for you.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:52.060
But just, if you could imagine
all of that complexity,

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.630
every single one of those components
can land as a data question.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:59.470
And so why I am here and
why our teams are here is to try

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:02.770
and think through ways to
make the student experience better,

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.240
to make the faculty
experience better,

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.010
to make the staff
experience better,

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:09.160
to make us work
more effectively, work more efficiently,

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:14.350
to make it so that the
people of Colorado have the best possible

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.700
university that they can have.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.530
So with that--

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.360
I'm loving this
chat, by the way

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.680
- Yeah, I love that--

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:26.870
I love that intro too.
But we forgot one thing.

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:29.170
What do you like to do
outside of work, as well?

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.930
- What do I like to
do outside of work? So

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:32.680
recently,

